1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:06,715
Who are you?

2
00:00:06,798 --> 00:00:10,301
Mr. Konta invited us over!

3
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:11,803
Isn't this just like…

4
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:13,680
Our very own reality dating show?

5
00:00:13,763 --> 00:00:16,599
I have a members-only service
where I post all about entrepreneurship.

6
00:00:16,683 --> 00:00:18,518
Would you like to subscribe to my service?

7
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:20,186
<i>I really don't want to get a sunburn.</i>

8
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:22,564
Could we swap seats?
Actually, should we just head inside?

9
00:00:22,647 --> 00:00:23,982
A Pinot Noir from Burgundy?

10
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:26,901
If you decant it a bit more,
the aroma will open up.

11
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:30,572
They sound smart when they talk,
but they feel weirdly shallow.

12
00:00:30,655 --> 00:00:32,657
They are completely empty inside.

13
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,576
Will Mr. Konta be back soon?

14
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:37,287
We came here
because we wanted to talk to him!

15
00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:40,707
Mr. Konta, the millionaire
who got to retire at a young age.

16
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,834
Say what?

17
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:49,382
TWO HOURS EARLIER

18
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,260
Radish? One hundred yen?

19
00:00:52,343 --> 00:00:53,303
These…

20
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:56,473
These are turnips. Red turnips.

21
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:02,854
Tatsumi Town feels much cooler
compared to Tokyo.

22
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,983
It seems inbound tourism
is driving up foreign demand around here,

23
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:08,985
making it the next big business spot!

24
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,029
A mentor at a seminar told me.

25
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:15,283
Seems like more Japanese business owners
are setting up villas here lately, too.

26
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,453
We need to expand our network
of wealthy contacts here

27
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:20,914
to outmaneuver the other young startups.

28
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,583
Though, at first glance,

29
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:26,544
there doesn't seem to be
anyone wealthy around here.

30
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:28,004
Idiot.

31
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:31,549
Real millionaires, they wear Uniqlo,

32
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:32,967
drive a Vitz,

33
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:35,804
and spend their weekends
eating at their villas.

34
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:38,723
Ordinary people just see them as ordinary.

35
00:01:38,807 --> 00:01:40,308
But we're different, right?

36
00:01:40,391 --> 00:01:42,185
As fellow business professionals,

37
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:45,230
we have to spot
the hidden aura within them.

38
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:46,439
But listen, like, today,

39
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,817
these tiny little turnips
were ridiculously cheap!

40
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,193
Radi? Radi…

41
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:51,361
Whatever, they're turnips!

42
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:54,572
They were practically giving them away!
So, I bought the entire stock!

43
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:57,700
Every single one! See ya later.

44
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:00,161
-He said "stock."
-What? She hung up already?

45
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:01,955
-Man, Midori…
-Go talk to him!

46
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:03,039
You go!

47
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:05,416
Excuse me.

48
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:08,419
Can we talk for a moment?

49
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:47,458
I knew the second I saw you
at the roadside station, Mr. Konta!

50
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:49,544
I knew you were someone extraordinary!

51
00:02:49,627 --> 00:02:50,879
Well, you know,

52
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:54,048
I do appear on TV a fair bit,
so yes, I guess.

53
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:58,094
So?

54
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:00,221
What made you so interested in me?

55
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:01,306
My young friends.

56
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:03,057
Did my aura give me away?

57
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:05,685
I guess I just couldn't hide it?

58
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:07,395
Yes! You have an aura!

59
00:03:07,478 --> 00:03:10,398
Please teach us the secret
to your success, Mr. Konta.

60
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:12,525
How you became a millionaire
at a young age!

61
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:13,526
What?

62
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:15,486
"Okuribito"?

63
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:19,824
Oh, that movie that won the Oscar?
I wasn't in <i>Departures</i>!

64
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:21,034
I didn't star in it!

65
00:03:21,826 --> 00:03:23,161
He's misunderstanding that?

66
00:03:23,244 --> 00:03:25,580
They weren't talking about the movie.

67
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:27,916
Konta is too stupid.

68
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:30,877
But seriously, this villa is incredible!

69
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:35,256
After coming here, we know this
is exactly the lifestyle we're aiming for!

70
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,884
Well, look at you guys. So passionate.

71
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:40,386
Are you all in the industry too?

72
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:42,263
Yes! We're still
just starting out, though.

73
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:44,641
You should have said so earlier!

74
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:46,935
I'll listen to whatever you want to share.

75
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:49,687
Then to start off,

76
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:53,816
what would you say
was your core strength in business?

77
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,777
Well, let's see…

78
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,821
I would say business is like…

79
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:00,073
taming tigers.

80
00:04:00,156 --> 00:04:01,282
What?

81
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:03,409
You were on <i>Business Tigers</i>?

82
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:08,373
BUSINESS TIGERS

83
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:11,501
I'm betting the full amount.

84
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:14,337
He didn't mean that show!

85
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:15,380
Wait, what did he mean?

86
00:04:15,463 --> 00:04:19,550
Konta was talking about
wrangling extras on set.

87
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:25,765
But lately, you know,
I'm not really in that phase anymore.

88
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:28,268
Incredible.

89
00:04:58,131 --> 00:05:00,925
Miraculously,
their conversations match up.

90
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:02,719
We need to clear up
their misunderstanding fast.

91
00:05:02,802 --> 00:05:05,179
They're all idiots, so they synced up.

92
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:07,223
Hey, Rinrin.

93
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:10,685
Could you go tell them that my brother
is just an unsuccessful actor?

94
00:05:10,768 --> 00:05:13,438
I've already lost interest
in those three morons.

95
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:15,315
You're already on a dating app!

96
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:21,279
Do we have more guests?

97
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:25,325
My brother dragged three people here.

98
00:05:27,076 --> 00:05:28,119
Oh!

99
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:29,579
Turnips!

100
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:32,915
So Konta was talking about radishes!

101
00:05:34,125 --> 00:05:36,002
Guess I'll make a salad.

102
00:05:36,085 --> 00:05:37,920
You should have some too.

103
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,172
We're doing a barbecue today!

104
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:41,382
No, I…

105
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:43,676
Oh, come on. Please stay and eat.

106
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:50,058
Okay.

107
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:54,145
Mr. Konta.

108
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:56,647
The three of us
actually post videos online.

109
00:05:56,731 --> 00:05:59,400
Would you consider appearing in one?

110
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:02,403
I'm sure tons of young people
want to hear your story!

111
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:06,991
Of course!
But make sure to film me from this angle.

112
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:09,452
This side of my face looks sharper.

113
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:10,369
Here, look.

114
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:11,662
I see it.

115
00:06:12,330 --> 00:06:14,749
They post videos? What kind of videos?

116
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:17,668
They sent me the link
when we were talking earlier.

117
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:20,088
They have 62 subscribers.

118
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:21,297
That's so few.

119
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,840
"The Three Growth Musketeers.

120
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:26,677
To aim for FIRE, you must take risks now!"

121
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:29,055
It's one of those seminar-style channels!

122
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,725
And so today, we asked Gen Z success story

123
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:36,521
Mr. Konta all about his work-life balance,
here at his villa!

124
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:38,564
See you in the next video!

125
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:41,275
Buh-bye!

126
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:45,571
Thank you so much!

127
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:48,407
-Thank you very much!
-How were my looks?

128
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:49,534
You were top-tier!

129
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:51,702
My look is on point today!

130
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:53,746
I'm totally serving!

131
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:56,207
Mr. Nishigami, you chopped the firewood?

132
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:57,333
Thank you!

133
00:06:57,416 --> 00:07:00,044
-You were on form!
-I'm going to burn lots.

134
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,796
-Thank you.
-Konta!

135
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:03,339
-Yes.
-We're about to start!

136
00:07:03,422 --> 00:07:04,423
Okay.

137
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:06,717
Oh, right. You should join us.

138
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:07,844
Wait, may we?

139
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:08,928
Thank you so much!

140
00:07:09,011 --> 00:07:10,388
Truly a winner at life!

141
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:12,765
Come on, you three.

142
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:16,102
Come on! Look at you, Tetsuro.
You're working super hard.

143
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:17,478
Seats.

144
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:26,779
Well then, here's to new encounters.

145
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:27,822
Cheers!

146
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:30,533
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

147
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:33,786
Thank you.

148
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,455
Welcome.

149
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:45,506
Is this pork?

150
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:46,966
It's not beef.

151
00:07:47,884 --> 00:07:49,802
My drink is all gone.

152
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:53,222
Huh? Is there any sauce? Sauce.

153
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:56,893
Hey, pitch in and help! What's with them?

154
00:07:56,976 --> 00:07:58,644
They're just sitting around!

155
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:01,731
They really don't think at all.

156
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:03,316
They are empty boys.

157
00:08:03,399 --> 00:08:07,195
Why did I even want
these three to like me?

158
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:17,413
Here! Start grilling your own food!
Thank you.

159
00:08:19,415 --> 00:08:20,541
Let's grill it.

160
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:21,959
Should we?

161
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:24,420
Watch out.

162
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:29,509
Are you members of any online communities?

163
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:32,345
Huh? Online communities?

164
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:34,764
No, we aren't in any.

165
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:37,683
Then how do you build your networks?

166
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:40,478
Never mind that, look at your chest.

167
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:41,395
There's a bug.

168
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,733
Oh, no! No, get it off!

169
00:08:45,816 --> 00:08:47,735
-Calm down.
-What is this?

170
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:49,737
-It's just a drone beetle.
-Gross!

171
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:51,447
Gross!

172
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:54,617
-You're cute.
-A cockroach, so gross.

173
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,410
Go on back to the forest.

174
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,163
No! The meat!

175
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:03,793
-Oh, crap…
-It's fine. I'll do it. Give.

176
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:12,969
It's hot.

177
00:09:14,095 --> 00:09:15,721
So hot!

178
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,641
So hot.

179
00:09:18,724 --> 00:09:19,559
You all right?

180
00:09:21,435 --> 00:09:22,895
Can't handle bugs.

181
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,438
Can't grill meat.

182
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:26,107
What is up with these guys?

183
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:27,650
Right?

184
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:29,944
They only came here to network.

185
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:42,957
Mr. Konta.
I am so, so glad I got to meet you today!

186
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,918
Same. I always want to support
young people working hard.

187
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:47,753
So, you can ask me for advice anytime.

188
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:51,465
I actually want to ask you
something right away.

189
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:53,467
Oh, that really is right away.

190
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:55,136
-What is it?
-Mr. Konta.

191
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:58,514
Would you be willing to invest in us?

192
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:07,690
-Invest?
-Yes!

193
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:09,317
-Me?
-Yes!

194
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,401
How much?

195
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:14,697
10,000 yen?

196
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:15,906
No.

197
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:16,991
1,000.

198
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:18,826
Oh, what?

199
00:10:18,909 --> 00:10:20,745
"Invest"? What an exaggeration!

200
00:10:20,828 --> 00:10:21,662
Sure.

201
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:23,080
Wait.

202
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:24,332
Really?

203
00:10:24,415 --> 00:10:25,333
Incredible.

204
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:28,002
I used to borrow money
from my seniors all the time.

205
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,380
Make sure you pay me back.

206
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:33,883
What?

207
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:35,051
No.

208
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,303
Not one of these.

209
00:10:37,386 --> 00:10:38,596
Not one?

210
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:41,557
What we mean
is an investment in our business.

211
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:42,808
Ten thousand of these.

212
00:10:44,518 --> 00:10:45,770
Say what?

213
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,396
That's ten million yen!

214
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:50,274
Are you out of your mind?
What are you saying?

215
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:51,317
I'm an actor.

216
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,861
No way I have that kind of money!
My savings are under 100,000.

217
00:10:53,944 --> 00:10:54,945
Wait.

218
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:56,530
You're an actor?

219
00:10:56,614 --> 00:10:57,657
Give it back.

220
00:10:59,575 --> 00:11:01,452
Don't look at my 1,000 yen.

221
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:03,746
Hey, look at this.

222
00:11:05,581 --> 00:11:06,916
SOUSAIDOU ACTORS OFFICE

223
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:09,085
This guy is an actor.

224
00:11:09,168 --> 00:11:10,795
So that means…

225
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:15,257
But you were talking stocks.

226
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:16,342
Stocks?

227
00:11:16,425 --> 00:11:19,512
Oh! I got a nice stock of turnips!
Did you not have the salad?

228
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:20,638
What?

229
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:22,932
So by stock, you meant these?

230
00:11:23,015 --> 00:11:26,018
Apparently, they're called radishes.
Or Raditz.

231
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:28,145
Like Goku's older brother.

232
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:29,980
I see.

233
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:32,608
It seems there was a misunderstanding.

234
00:11:32,691 --> 00:11:35,486
So Mr. Konta, you aren't rich?

235
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:37,154
Of course not!

236
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:42,910
This is the worst.

237
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:45,287
I'm covered in bug bites everywhere.

238
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:46,330
It's the worst.

239
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:48,082
Jeez, so many bugs!

240
00:12:05,307 --> 00:12:06,559
The meat!

241
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,445
Are you okay?

242
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:26,912
Excuse me.

243
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:29,373
What?

244
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:34,336
-Oh, man!
-That was close!

245
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:35,838
Can we salvage this?

246
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:37,673
You should have hedged the risk.

247
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:41,093
Just go home already! You total airheads!

248
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:44,346
From now on, you guys better
call yourselves "The Empty Boys"!

249
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:46,765
"The Empty Boys"?

250
00:12:46,849 --> 00:12:47,850
It's fine.

251
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:51,562
An empty head just means
you can stuff more dreams into it!

252
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:56,859
Well then…

253
00:12:56,942 --> 00:12:58,360
Thanks for the food.

254
00:12:58,444 --> 00:12:59,945
Clean up after yourselves!

255
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,197
Don't come back!

256
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:04,241
Oh, there are tons of bugs
on the way out. So here.

257
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:05,951
-Thank you.
-You can have it.

258
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:06,994
Are you sure?

259
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:08,537
Thank you.

260
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:10,831
-Bye. See you again.
-We'll come again.

261
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:12,082
Thank you!

262
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:22,635
Still, I don't think I have any right
to look down on those guys.

263
00:13:22,718 --> 00:13:23,636
What?

264
00:13:24,261 --> 00:13:26,347
I think I might be empty too.

265
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:29,683
When it comes to work and romance.

266
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:32,144
And intelligence?

267
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:38,400
But today, I think I finally figured out
who I should really be looking at.

268
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:40,611
What's with you?

269
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:49,870
Konta.

270
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:50,913
Let me help you!

271
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:52,414
Oh, Rinrin, thanks.

272
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,375
Watch out for the ash.

273
00:13:54,458 --> 00:13:55,668
-Got it.
-All right.

274
00:14:37,835 --> 00:14:39,003
Mr. Nishigami!

275
00:14:40,963 --> 00:14:43,841
Thank you for earlier.

276
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:46,844
It was nothing.

277
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:49,388
Well…

278
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,809
I am really grateful.

279
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:56,854
Mr. Nishigami…

280
00:14:57,938 --> 00:15:01,358
You protected me from the fire.

281
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:03,485
Well…

282
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:06,739
I…

283
00:15:06,822 --> 00:15:08,365
Please excuse me.

284
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:14,663
Mr. Nishigami!

285
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:19,877
See you tomorrow!

286
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:43,984
Look at this.

287
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,694
Oh, the video from the other day?

288
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:46,946
They actually uploaded it.

289
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:47,905
COMMENTS

290
00:15:47,988 --> 00:15:49,990
-What?
-What's with these comments?

291
00:15:50,074 --> 00:15:52,618
Huh? Why is everyone talking about stocks?

292
00:15:52,701 --> 00:15:54,286
Because they're all idiots.

293
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:56,372
Hey, look at the channel name.

294
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:59,500
"The Empty Boys: We're Gonna Smash It!"

295
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:01,210
Huh? I don't get it.

296
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:04,880
Well, they weren't dating material,
but maybe they're decent guys?

297
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:06,256
Nope. Not at all!

298
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:08,467
So harsh. Brutal.

299
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:19,061
WE SPOKE TO SUCCESSFUL BUSINESSMAN
KONTA HOSHINO!

300
00:16:19,144 --> 00:16:21,355
-Isn't this hilarious?
-Yeah.

301
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:25,025
I stumbled on it while looking
at a channel run by my college friends!

302
00:16:25,109 --> 00:16:26,652
This guy isn't bad…

303
00:16:27,403 --> 00:16:30,614
You know, he might actually
be pretty interesting.

304
00:16:54,763 --> 00:16:55,723
On me?

305
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:57,099
<i>Did something happen to Konta?</i>

306
00:16:57,182 --> 00:16:59,351
<i>I bet he failed another audition.</i>

307
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:01,520
<i>Do you know a show called</i>
Document Memoreal<i>?</i>

308
00:17:01,603 --> 00:17:03,564
They want to do a feature on me.

309
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:04,940
Say what?

310
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:06,900
-Let me carry that.
-Mr. Nishigami.

311
00:17:06,984 --> 00:17:09,278
I'm happy for Mr. Konta.

312
00:17:09,903 --> 00:17:12,698
Good morning.
I'm Torihara from <i>Document Memoreal</i>.

313
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:13,907
Why those outfits and makeup?

314
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:15,367
We might be on camera too.

315
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:17,036
I look forward to working with you all!

316
00:17:17,661 --> 00:17:20,581
-He's getting carried away.
-Is he really going to be okay?

317
00:17:20,664 --> 00:17:23,083
<i>He thinks he'll go viral</i>
<i>and become popular.</i>

318
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,585
<i>You're being tricked.</i>

319
00:17:24,668 --> 00:17:28,922
<i>I'm the actor, Konta Hoshino.</i>

320
00:17:29,006 --> 00:17:29,965
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
